Legal Specification — GODSPEED Bulk‑Connect Permission Model

Bulk‑connect is lawful because connection does not grant access. Permissions are granted only at time of use, satisfying GDPR, CCPA, HIPAA, SOC 2, ISO 27001, and NIST Zero‑Trust. This model separates identity boundaries from connector attachment, enabling safe, scalable AI deployment.
# Architecture — GODSPEED Bulk‑Connect Permission Model

Two‑Stage Model:
1. Connect: Attach all tools with zero permissions.
2. Permission: Grant access only when a tool is used.

States:
- Connected
- Pending
- Active
- Revoked

This architecture mirrors OAuth, Azure AD, Google Workspace, AWS IAM, and mobile app permission flows.
